      <workList xml:id="workDesc_245c9730">
         <work xml:id="work_idaee73eb1">
            <identifier label="SchW" xml:id="identifier_7668289b">A1:Coll.001</identifier>
            <title xml:id="title_idf076f328" xml:lang="it">IV concerti, à cembalo oblig., 2 flauti, 2 violini, viola e basso</title>
            <contributor xml:id="respStmt_00399c56">
               <persName role="composer" xml:id="persName_idca17b8af">Johann Adolph Scheibe</persName>
            </contributor>
            <history xml:id="history_id8aa41275">
               <p xml:id="idm60">These four works which presumably have been lost appear in two of the Breitkopf catalogues (1761 and 1763) of which the second one includes incipits. It seems likely that Breitkopf might have obtained them in 1761 from the estate of <persName xml:id="idm61" auth.uri="http://www.viaf.org" auth="VIAF" role="">Carl Gotthelf Gerlach</persName>, cantor of Neukirche in Leipzig, or perhaps from the collegium musicum. It is also possible, however, that Scheibe sent them directly to the publishers at an earlier date. The concertos are most likely also those listed in the auction catalogue of 1836 (lot 1280 (1)).</p>
            </history>
            <langUsage xml:id="langUsage_42b1f324">
               <language xml:id="en">English</language>
               <language xml:id="it">Italian</language>
            </langUsage>
            <biblList xml:id="biblList_257N20127">
